  "id": "transitivity",
  "term": "transitivity",
  "definition": "In this context, transitivity is a discourse-analysis framework used to examine how language assigns roles in actions, such as who is presented as acting and who is acted upon. By analyzing patterns like Actor and Goal in clauses, it helps show how a person, group, or place is represented as having more or less agency over time.",
